0..73 Comment "// Abstraction in rule terms (Gabbay and Mathijssen, _Nominal (universal)"
74..151 Comment "// algebra_, JLC 2009; Fernández and Gabbay, _Nominal rewriting_, I&C 2007)."
152..229 Comment "// At a port written `bind (a : N) . T`, a rule writes `bind a . t`: the atom"
230..305 Comment "// `a` abstracted over the term `t`. Admission re-mints every abstraction\'s"
306..379 Comment "// atom by its depth among the abstractions above it, so `bind a . t` and"
380..457 Comment "// `bind b . t` are one term to matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s"
458..536 Comment "// replay alike. The value of `Theory` keeps each atom as written, as it keeps"
537..609 Comment "// a rule\'s variables. The signature is `bind-port.gandr`\'s restriction."
611..685 Comment "/// Scope extrusion: a restriction over one side of a parallel composition"
686..759 Comment "/// encloses both. `q` moves under the restriction, so the law states `a`"
760..835 Comment "/// fresh for it (`freshness.gandr`). The checker orients the law, finds no"
836..889 Comment "/// critical pair and the kernel replays the verdict."
